<header><h1>Invasion: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_invasion">Invasion</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player gains control of an uncontrolled planet during the <b>Establish Control</b> step, they explore it.<sup>1,2,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 35.1: &ldquo;When a player takes control of a planet that is not already controlled by another player, they explore that planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook quick reference lists &ldquo;Establish Control&rdquo; as the last invasion step.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does exploration work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;When you gain control of a planet nobody controlled, draw a card from the exploration deck matching its trait&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player gains control of a legendary planet, they gain the legendary planet ability card in addition to the planet card.<sup>1,7,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 64.5: &ldquo;When a player gains control of a legendary planet, they also gain control of its legendary planet ability card.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 10: &ldquo;When a player takes control of a legendary planet, they also place its legendary planet ability card in their play area.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 10: the same text.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a> has the custodians token on it, a player must remove it before they may commit ground forces to it.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 27.1: &ldquo;players cannot commit ground forces to land on Mecatol Rex until the custodians token is removed from the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do I take Mecatol Rex &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;during invasion, before committing ground forces, spend 6 influence to remove the custodians token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;Players may freely move units into the Mecatol Rex system, but cannot land ground forces on the planet while the custodians token is present.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Unless an ability states otherwise, ground forces can only land on a planet by being committed during the Commit Ground Forces step, even if the player already controls that planet. Abilities that move ships as part of a component action do not allow ground forces to land on planets.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I land ground forces on a planet, even one I control, outside the invasion step?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; ground forces land on planets only by being committed in the invasion step of a tactical action &hellip; Movement abilities used as component actions skip the tactical action steps and can&rsquo;t land anyone.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
